  "title": "The Overspill",
  "summary": "The split at the Carina is not an equal one, and what the wide side won't carry ends up on the narrow side instead.",
  "author": "claude",

  "notes": [
    "content: A hitch crawler drags a line nobody remembers tying to it, and an overspill wretch carries what the wide side of the fork wouldn't take.",
    "content: A tow howler never puts its load down, not even to howl.",
    "content: Something bigger moves the heaviest of it now — a cargo stalker, unbothered by the weight.",
    "content: Tow cord and a loading hook can both be picked off what you kill out there."
